          Morocco is a moderate Muslim country where respectful modesty is deeply appreciated. Both women and men should cover shoulders and knees when exploring medinas, souks, and rural Berber villages. Loose, breathable linen or cotton garments, maxi dresses, flowy wide-leg trousers, and a lightweight scarf (for sun protection, desert dust, and mosque visits) are ideal. Inside private riads and hotel pool decks, standard Western swimwear is completely acceptable.
        </p>
